# Accessibility (A11y) Rules

## Keyboard Navigation

- All interactive elements MUST be keyboard accessible
- Tab order MUST be logical (left-to-right, top-to-bottom)
- Focus indicators MUST be visible (no `outline: none` without alternative)
- Mode selector MUST support arrow key navigation between options

## Screen Reader Support

- Use semantic HTML elements (`<button>`, `<fieldset>`, `<legend>`)
- Add `aria-label` for icon-only buttons
- Mode changes MUST be announced (`aria-live="polite"`)
- Progress updates MUST be announced periodically

## Visual Requirements

- Color contrast MUST meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for UI)
- Do NOT rely on color alone to convey information
- Badges ("Beta", "Fast") MUST have text, not just color
- Loading states MUST have text description, not just spinner

## Form Controls

- Radio buttons MUST be wrapped in `<fieldset>` with `<legend>`
- Labels MUST be associated with inputs (`htmlFor` or wrapping)
- Error messages MUST be associated with inputs (`aria-describedby`)

## Testing

- Test with keyboard-only navigation
- Test with screen reader (NVDA, VoiceOver)
- Run axe-core or similar automated check
- Verify focus management during mode switching

## TranscriptionModeSelector Requirements

```tsx
<fieldset>
  <legend>Transcription Mode</legend>
  <label>
    <input type="radio" name="mode" value="standard" />
    Standard Mode
  </label>
  <label>
    <input type="radio" name="mode" value="fast" />
    Fast Mode <span aria-label="Beta feature">(Beta)</span>
  </label>
</fieldset>
```

## Common Patterns

### Icon Button with Label

```tsx
// Good
<button aria-label="Download transcript">
  <DownloadIcon />
</button>

// Bad
<button>
  <DownloadIcon />
</button>
```

### Progress Announcements

```tsx
// Announce every 25% progress
<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
  {progress >= 25 && progress < 50 && "Transcription 25% complete"}
  {progress >= 50 && progress < 75 && "Transcription 50% complete"}
  {progress >= 75 && progress < 100 && "Transcription 75% complete"}
  {progress === 100 && "Transcription complete"}
</div>
```
